# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
pytest-of-*/

# maturin / setuptools-rust build artifacts
python/odock/*.pyd
python/odock/*.so
python/odock/*.dll

# Local scratch
/reference
/scratch
/out
/.rust-tmp
*.log
*.npy
/tmp*

# A release snapshot of this repository, staged at its own root by the release
# process. It is not part of the project and must not be committed or packaged
# (`tools/inspect_dist.py` fails if a root `odock/` reaches an artefact).
/odock/

# Internal working documents, explicitly not for publication: `odck.md` is the
# requirements brief and `DELIVERY.md` is the hand-over superseded by
# docs/VALIDATION.md. They stay on disk; they must not be committed and maturin's
# `exclude` keeps them out of the artefacts, with the inspect tool as the backstop.
#
# `docs/INTERFACES.md` was the frozen integration contract between workstreams.
# It is an internal document with no meaning to a reader of a published
# repository, so it was moved out of the published `docs/` set (it now lives in
# the ignored `out/` scratch area). The path stays reserved here so that a
# reinstated contract cannot leak by accident either. `docs/VALIDATION.md`, the
# published replacement for the hand-over, is NOT ignored.
/odck.md
/DELIVERY.md
/docs/INTERFACES.md

# Structures fetched while poking at a system belong in tests/data/, which is
# where the tests and the benchmark look for them (`--data-dir` defaults to it);
# a PDB at the repository root is a stray. Already-tracked files stay tracked.
/*.pdb

# The demo directory *is* published: `demo/README.md` documents it, the README
# walk-through uses it, and the release checker's declared paths expect it. What
# must not ship is the vendored AutoDock Vina binary the CLI walk-through used
# for comparison — 1.2 MB of third-party, Windows-only executable — so the rule
# targets exactly that file rather than the data around it.
#
# This used to be `/demo/*` plus `!/demo/library.smi`. Ignoring the whole
# directory made the hand-maintained screening library invisible (hence the
# exception) and silently dropped 18 files that the release is supposed to
# contain, which `out/verify/release_check.py` reported as a failure. Ignore the
# binary, not the data.
/demo/**/vina.exe

# Local release backups (archives of published versions)
/backup/
